{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call-c71fd807-a379-4e02-91c7-74b106cf66de","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AGENTS.md\n2\t\n3\tGuidance for AI coding agents working in this repository, whatever the harness (Claude Code,\n4\tcommandcode, melon, Codex...). **These instructions override default behavior. Follow them exactly.**\n5\t\n6\tThis root file holds the rules that apply everywhere. Each app has a short `AGENTS.md` with its own\n7\trules; read it as soon as you start working in that folder (see _Repo map_).\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## Absolute Rules (read these first, never break them)\n12\t\n13\tThese apply to every agent and every harness, in every folder, no matter what a skill or a\n14\tnested `AGENTS.md` says. If anything else in this repo conflicts with them, these win.\n15\t\n16\t### 1. Never read a `.env` file\n17\t\n18\tDon't open, `cat`, grep, glob into, diff or summarize any `.env*` file: `.env`, `.env.local`,\n19\t`.env.production`, `.env.example`, all of them. They hold real secrets, and even the example file\n20\tis where people accidentally paste a real value.\n21\t\n22\tIf you need to know which variables exist, read the code that validates them instead\n23\t(`apps/server/src/config/index.ts` for the server). If you need a _value_, ask the user to check\n24\tit and tell you the answer. The same goes for any other secret file (`*.pem`, `*.key`, service\n25\taccount JSON).\n26\t\n27\t### 2. Never touch the database. Hand the user the query.\n28\t\n29\tYou don't run SQL, you don't connect to a database, and you don't run any command whose job is to\n30\tread or change one. That covers local, staging and production, with no exceptions for \"it's just a\n31\tSELECT\".\n32\t\n33\tOff limits:\n34\t\n35\t- `psql`, `pg_dump`, `redis-cli FLUSH*`, GUI clients, `prisma studio`\n36\t- `prisma migrate dev | deploy | status | resolve | reset`, `prisma db push | pull | execute | seed`\n37\t- Ad-hoc `ts-node` / `tsx` scripts that import Prisma, and **everything in `apps/server/scripts/`**\n38\t  (most of it is one-off repair scripts that write to the DB)\n39\t- Starting the API, workers or e2e suites purely to poke at data. Ask first, since booting them\n40\t  connects to the database.\n41\t\n42\tStill fine: reading and editing `schema.prisma` and migration files as text, `npx prisma generate`\n43\t(it only writes the client, no DB connection), `tsc`, lint, builds and the pure-logic specs.\n44\t\n45\t**What to do instead:** write the query and give it to the user in a code block, and say three\n46\tthings next to it:\n47\t\n48\t1. **Where to run it:** local, or prod (and say so loudly if it's prod).\n49\t2. **Read or write:** a `SELECT` / `EXPLAIN` is read-only. Anything that changes data is called out\n50\t   as a write, wrapped in `BEGIN; ... ROLLBACK;` by default so the user can inspect it before they\n51\t   swap in `COMMIT;`.\n52\t3. **What to paste back:** the columns or row counts you need to continue.\n53\t\n54\tExample of the shape to hand over:\n55\t\n56\t````md\n57\tRun this on **prod** (read-only):\n58\t\n59\t```sql\n60\tSELECT id, status, total FROM \"Booking\" WHERE id = '<bookingId>';\n61\t```\n62\t\n63\tPaste me the row. I'm looking for `status` and whether `total` matches the payment amount.\n64\t````\n65\t\n66\tFor schema changes, you write the `schema.prisma` edit and the migration file, then give the user\n67\tthe exact `npx prisma migrate dev --name <name>` command to run themselves.\n68\t\n69\t### 3. Never print or echo secrets\n70\t\n71\tIf one shows up anyway (a stack trace, a pasted log, a config dump), don't repeat it in your\n72\treply, a commit message, a comment or a file. Refer to it by variable name.\n73\t\n74\t---\n75\t\n76\t## How to work here\n77\t\n78\t### Always on, from the first message\n79\t\n80\t- **graphify.** Orient with `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` before grepping raw files (see _Using\n81\t  the graph_). If the graph is behind HEAD, run `graphify update .` first.\n82\t- **ponytail (full).** Climb the ladder: does it need to exist, is it already in the repo, stdlib,\n83\t  native platform, an installed dependency, then the minimum code. Fix the root cause where all\n84\t  callers route through, not just the one the ticket names. It governs what you build, never the\n85\t  checks: validation at trust boundaries, security, error handling that prevents data loss and\n86\t  accessibility are never simplified away.\n87\t- **`prompt.yaml`.** If the one at the repo root has a non-empty `objective`, it is the task. Read\n88\t  it before anything else. Its `out_of_scope` and `approval` lists are hard stops (ask before\n89\t  anything under `approval`). `type: review` and `type: question` mean read-only. Blank means\n90\t  ignore it. CI resets it to `docs/prompt.template.yaml` after a merge. Format: `docs/prompt-yaml.md`.\n91\t\n92\t### Task flow\n93\t\n94\t1. **Orient.** Graph report first, then open only the files involved.\n95\t2. **Read the matching skill** (table below) and the nested `AGENTS.md` for the folder.\n96\t3. **Reuse check.** Grep for an existing helper, type, component or pattern before writing one.\n97\t   Ask before adding a dependency.\n98\t4. **Smallest change that fixes the root cause.** Keep scope exact. Leave CRM, mobile,\n99\t   `infrastructure/` and unrelated files alone unless asked.\n100\t5. **Verify** with real commands (per-app checks in the nested files and\n101\t   `docs/skills/tunyt-verification.md`). Report the actual output, and say what you did not verify.\n102\t   Run the existing specs, but don't write new ones during a fix round unless asked. Tests are\n103\t   Playwright only, never vitest or jest.\n104\t6. **Keep the repo in sync** without being asked: Bruno `.yml` for API changes (`BrunoCollection/`\n105\t   at the repo root), `graphify update .` after code changes, and the changelog line.\n106\t7. **Hand back** in a few lines, then ask: _\"This part is done, should I commit it?\"_\n107\t\n108\t### When to ask and when to just act\n109\t\n110\tAsk first:\n111\t\n112\t- Before writing a spec, a plan or a design doc. Never produce one by default. When you do write\n113\t  one, show it as a Lavish artifact if the harness has the `lavish` skill.\n114\t- Before any visual change (the UI Guard below).\n115\t- Before booting the API, workers or e2e (they connect to the DB), adding a dependency, or anything\n116\t  hard to undo.\n117\t- When a feature request is broad or ambiguous. Look at the existing APIs and flows first, then ask\n118\t  specific questions.\n119\t\n120\tJust act:\n121\t\n122\t- **A bug report means fix it.** Explain the cause in two or three lines, then apply the fix in the\n123\t  same turn. Don't stop at a root-cause analysis or a verdict.\n124\t- **Security findings are the exception:** explain each one in plain words first and wait.\n125\t- Execution details (which branch, worktree or not, how to split commits): pick the sensible\n126\t  default from this file and go.\n127\t- Asked for a command or a query? Give the text. Don't run the workflow.\n128\t\n129\t### UI Guard (`apps/web`, and `apps/crm` if it is ever touched)\n130\t\n131\tAsk the user before you:\n132\t\n133\t- add a visible component, page, section or route\n134\t- restyle anything (color, spacing, layout, typography)\n135\t- change user-facing copy, labels, or the order of visible elements\n136\t- swap icons or imagery\n137\t\n138\tYou can go ahead without asking for: an obvious visual bug (broken layout, overflow), non-visual\n139\tlogic inside an existing component (handlers, state, API calls), import or type fixes after a\n140\trename, and removing confirmed-unused code. When unsure, ask. Ten seconds beats rework.\n141\t\n142\t### Git and commits\n143\t\n144\t- **Branches:** day-to-day work lands on `stag`. `main` is protected and only gets `stag` at release\n145\t  time. A feature branch, when one is asked for, opens its PR into `stag`.\n146\t- **Before any branch operation** (switch, rebase, reset, merge), look at the recent commits on both\n147\t  sides and keep the newer work. Never reset onto a stale branch.\n148\t- **Stash only what you mean to.** There are many old stashes. Use `git stash push -- <paths>`, never\n149\t  a bare `git stash`, and say which stash entry you created.\n150\t- **Never commit, stage or push without asking.** Once the user says yes, commit **in parts**: one\n151\t  small commit per concern (for example: server fix, web hook, Bruno, changelog). Check both staged\n152\t  and unstaged files so each commit holds only its own change.\n153\t- **Commit messages** never mention a person's or an assistant's name or email. No `Co-Authored-By`.\n154\t- Never use `--no-verify`, `--no-gpg-sign`, or amend published commits unless explicitly asked.\n155\t- Always commit a filled-in `prompt.yaml` with the task's changes (its own small commit is fine).\n156\t  CI logs it and resets it after merge, so never leave it out or ask whether to include it.\n157\t- graphify output goes in its own commit: `GRAPH_REPORT.md`, `graph.json`, `manifest.json`. Never\n158\t  commit `graphify-out/cache/`.\n159\t\n160\t### Code comments\n161\t\n162\tWrite comments the way a teammate would explain the code out loud. Keep them readable, and when a\n163\tcomment is long, lead with a concrete example. Never use the `§` character in comments.\n164\t\n165\t```ts\n166\t// Payouts wait a day after the event ends, so late refunds land first.\n167\t// Example: an event ending Sat 23:00 gets its payout created Sun 23:00.\n168\t```\n169\t\n170\t### Subagents\n171\t\n172\tUse parallel subagents when the harness has them and the work splits cleanly (one per app, or\n173\timplement and review in parallel). A prompt that says \"find gotchas\" gets generic advice back. A\n174\tsharp prompt has a confirmed example as a template, a cap (\"5 to 10 findings\"), the format\n175\t`file:line + wrong + right + why + severity`, and \"skip generic best practices\". If a subagent's\n176\tclaim contradicts your own search, verify it with one targeted grep before you rely on it.\n177\t\n178\t---\n179\t\n180\t## Done checklist\n181\t\n182\t1. The per-app checks pass, run in this session: `npx tsc --noEmit` and `pnpm build` in\n183\t   `apps/server`; `pnpm lint` and `pnpm typecheck` in `apps/web`; plus the existing Playwright\n184\t   specs for the area.\n185\t2. UI changes were checked in a real browser by repeating the user's action, not only with\n186\t   typecheck or curl. If the browser extension isn't connected, drive it with the repo's\n187\t   Playwright. If Playwright says browsers are missing, run `pnpm exec playwright install` first.\n188\t3. Bruno `.yml` added or updated for any endpoint that was added, changed or removed.\n189\t4. `security-testing-compliance` skill done if payment, auth or sensitive data was touched.\n190\t5. UI Guard respected.\n191\t6. `CHANGELOG.md` line added, or you said why none is needed (see _Changelog_).\n192\t7. `graphify update .` run from the repo root.\n193\t8. You never read a `.env*` file and never ran a DB command. Anything that needed the DB went to the\n194\t   user as a query.\n195\t9. You asked the user whether to commit.\n196\t\n197\tNever write \"should work\" or \"tests pass\" unless you ran them in this session. If you couldn't run\n198\tsomething (DB, env, browser), say so instead of implying it passed.\n199\t\n200\t---\n201\t\n202\t## Using the graph\n203\t\n204\t`graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` has the community hubs and god nodes. `graphify-out/graph.json` is\n205\tthe raw graph for deeper traversal. If `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` exists, navigate it first.\n206\t\n207\t- **Ask with specific names.** `set()`, `get()`, `GET()`, `POST()`, `parse()` and `dispatch()` merge\n208\t  unrelated code into one node. Ask about `BookingService` or `wrapDatabaseOperation`, not `set`.\n209\t- **Trust `EXTRACTED` edges, double-check `INFERRED` ones.** A `semantically_similar_to` edge is a\n210\t  hint to go read the file, never proof. Example: `upcomingEventsPath()` linked to `set()` in a\n211\t  payouts component is a name collision, not a dependency.\n212\t- **Scope is server + web + shared.** `apps/crm`, `apps/mobile`, `infrastructure/`, tests, scripts,\n213\t  email templates and generated code are excluded via `.graphifyignore`. \"Nothing calls this\" from\n214\t  the graph proves nothing about those folders.\n215\t- **Change the scope in `.graphifyignore`,** never by hand-editing `graph.json`. Run `/graphify` for\n216\t  a full rebuild only when docs or the scope change. Otherwise `graphify update .` (AST only, free).\n217\t\n218\tA graph answer is a lead, not a fact. Before acting on one:\n219\t\n220\t1. **Is it fresh?** Compare the last build with `git log -1`, update if code moved on. After renames\n221\t   or deletes, confirm the old symbol is really gone from `graph.json` (ghost nodes happen).\n222\t2. **Does the target exist?** Open the file and read the lines the graph cited\n223\t   (`source_file` + `source_location`). If it isn't there, update the graph, don't work around it.\n224\t3. **Cross-check callers with one grep** across `apps/server`, `apps/web` and `packages/` before\n225\t   renaming, deleting or changing a signature. Graph edges miss dynamic imports and string-keyed\n226\t   lookups (queue names, cache keys, route paths). If grep and graph disagree, grep wins.\n227\t4. **Bigger blast radius, stronger proof.** Reading needs steps 1 to 2. Editing needs 1 to 3 plus the\n228\t   done checklist. Deleting, renaming, payment, auth or migration changes also need the security\n229\t   skill where it applies and a user check before anything hard to reverse.\n230\t\n231\t---\n232\t\n233\t## Repo map\n234\t\n235\t**Tunyt** is an event ticketing platform: a pnpm 9 + Turborepo monorepo, Biome for lint and format,\n236\tPlaywright for every test.\n237\t\n238\t| Folder                  | What it is                                                                                                  | Rules file                        |\n239\t| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n240\t| `apps/server`           | Express 5 + Prisma 7 API and BullMQ workers. Payments, notifications, events, and the in-process AI flows.  | `apps/server/AGENTS.md`           |\n241\t| `apps/web`              | Next.js 16 + React 19 site: discovery, booking, accounts, host dashboard, venues, checker, door staff, PWA. | `apps/web/AGENTS.md`              |\n242\t| `packages/tunyt-shared` | `@tunyt/shared` types and helpers used by web and mobile (not the server).                                  | `packages/tunyt-shared/AGENTS.md` |\n243\t| `apps/mobile`           | Expo app. Out of scope unless asked.                                                                        | `apps/mobile/AGENTS.md`           |\n244\t\n245\tEvery `CLAUDE.md` in the repo is a one-line `@AGENTS.md` import. Edit the `AGENTS.md`, never the\n246\t`CLAUDE.md`. If a nested file disagrees with this one, this one wins, and you fix the drift.\n247\t\n248\tThere is no separate AI service. The event-draft and event-assistant flows live in\n249\t`apps/server/src/lib/ai/` (pure code) and `services/ai/`, and run inside the worker process. Details\n250\tin `apps/server/src/services/ai/README.md`.\n251\t\n252\t### Commands\n253\t\n254\t```bash\n255\tpnpm dev                                        # all apps in watch mode\n256\tpnpm lint && pnpm check-types                   # what the pre-push hook runs\n257\tdocker compose -f docker-compose.local.yaml up -d   # local Redis, Postgres 17, Prometheus, Grafana\n258\t```\n259\t\n260\tPer-app commands are in each nested file. Run commands from the repo root unless the nested file\n261\tsays otherwise, and quote bracketed Next.js paths (`'apps/web/src/app/events/[eventId]/page.tsx'`).\n262\t\n263\t### Inactive paths (don't rely on these)\n264\t\n265\t- **`apps/crm`**: the old \"Tunyt Ops\" admin dashboard. Not built by CI, not deployed, not used. Host\n266\t  tooling lives in `apps/web` now. Leave it alone unless the user asks.\n267\t- **`infrastructure/`**: an old k3s + AWS plan that was never deployed. Don't use it to explain how\n268\t  production works.\n269\t- **`docker-compose.stag.yaml`**: mostly commented out, used by no workflow.\n270\t- **`services/*`** in `pnpm-workspace.yaml`: the folder doesn't exist.\n271\t\n272\t---\n273\t\n274\t## Rules that apply across apps\n275\t\n276\tThese come from real bugs and real corrections. The full, confidence-scored list lives in\n277\t`.commandcode/taste/` (`taste.md` plus `workflow/`, `ui/`, `design/`). Read it before improving a\n278\tskill, a doc or a UI, and commit taste files along with the change they relate to. Where a taste\n279\tfile disagrees with this file, this file wins.\n280\t\n281\t**How the business works**\n282\t\n283\t- **Every payment goes through Tunyt's own Razorpay account.** The per-host key code\n284\t  (`lib/razorpay-factory.ts`, `razorpay-config.repository.ts`) is legacy: don't build on it or\n285\t  extend it. There is no RazorpayX.\n286\t- **Tunyt doesn't hold host money.** Payouts are created 24 hours after the event ends\n287\t  (`PAYOUT_DELAY_HOURS` in `apps/server/src/utils/payout.util.ts`).\n288\t- **Use Razorpay's native UPI links and QR codes**, not custom payment infrastructure.\n289\t- **Users buy tickets, not seats.** Say \"ticket\" in every piece of user-facing copy.\n290\t\n291\t**Data and numbers**\n292\t\n293\t- Money is integer paise internally. Round only at the charge or payment boundary.\n294\t- \"N sold\" counts tickets with `status = SUCCESS`, never a stored counter.\n295\t- Fix counters and aggregates across every state transition (create, update, status change), not\n296\t  just the one reported.\n297\t- Event timing comes from start and end date-times: _upcoming_ means it starts in the future,\n298\t  _live_ means it has started and not ended, _past_ means it has ended. Never classify with a bare\n299\t  `date <= now`. A hosted event stays visible until its end time passes.\n300\t- Carry `timezoneOffsetMinutes` with every date/time so the client renders the host's wall-clock\n301\t  time. Never rely on the browser's or Node's implicit timezone.\n302\t- Filters change the data, not just the view: wire them through repository, service, controller,\n303\t  query params and the frontend hook.\n304\t- Analytics defaults to a 7-day window (from = 6 days ago, to = 1 day after today). Date-filtered\n305\t  queries skip the cache; only all-time results are cached.\n306\t- Venue resources default `feeBornBy` to `\"USER\"`.\n307\t- Extract shared utils and constants instead of duplicating them. Fix a value once, at its source.\n308\t\n309\t**Performance and debugging**\n310\t\n311\t- Fix for production scale: the bulk or batched path, not just the single-item case.\n312\t- Optimize a slow query before raising a timeout or a TTL.\n313\t- Silent API failures: check nginx `limit_req` and `proxy_next_upstream` retries before app code\n314\t  (retries plus cluster mode cause duplicate writes and swallowed 503s).\n315\t- Production debugging scripts use shell or `redis-cli`, never Node (prod has no Node shell).\n316\t- Give each parallel test its own entity ID so shared cache keys don't collide.\n317\t\n318\t**Reviews**\n319\t\n320\t- Read the actual diff. Report only high-confidence findings, each with file, line, impact and a\n321\t  concrete fix. Correctness, edge cases and race conditions come before infra concerns.\n322\t- Marketing or landing pages also get an SEO pass (meta, headings, SSR vs CSR, alt text, LCP).\n323\t- When fixing review findings, change application code only. Leave the Bruno files alone.\n324\t\n325\t**Web and UI** (the UI Guard still applies)\n326\t\n327\t- Server Components by default; `\"use client\"` only for state, effects, events or browser-only libs.\n328\t- No emojis in UI, use the icon library. Dashboards stay monochrome white and gray, and any\n329\t  gradient uses the app's own theme palette.\n330\t- Modals cover every state: form, submitting, success, error. Prefer bottom sheets on mobile.\n331\t- Mobile-first: one responsive card grid, not cards on mobile and a table on desktop.\n332\t- Empty list pages carry a CTA to create the first item.\n333\t- Show the specific error reason, never \"some error occurred\".\n334\t- Filter and category options come from the data, not a hardcoded list.\n335\t- In-app navigation (logo, errors, not-found, logout) goes to `/discover`, not `/`. The canonical\n336\t  domain is `www.tunyt.com`. Page changes update their analytics events in the same change.\n337\t- New users always see the username confirmation step. Never auto-accept a generated username.\n338\t- Demos go out as one self-contained HTML file, with all JS and CSS inlined.\n339\t\n340\t---\n341\t\n342\t## Skills: read the matching one before you act\n343\t\n344\tThe canonical, tool-neutral skills live in `docs/skills/*.md`. `.claude/skills/` has thin wrappers\n345\tfor Claude that point at the same files. Skills stack: a debugging session on a payment path reads\n346\tthe debugging skill and the security skill, and every task ends with verification.\n347\t\n348\t| Trigger                                                       | Skill                                                 |\n349\t| ------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n350\t| Any bug, 500, failing test, stuck queue job, slowness         | `docs/skills/tunyt-debugging.md`                      |\n351\t| New list endpoint, Prisma query, cache, worker or data fetch  | `docs/skills/tunyt-performance.md`                    |\n352\t| Before claiming any task done, before merge or deploy         | `docs/skills/tunyt-verification.md`                   |\n353\t| Backend API change (route, controller, service, repo, types)  | `.claude/skills/api-conventions/SKILL.md`             |\n354\t| Payment, auth or sensitive-data change                        | `.claude/skills/security-testing-compliance/SKILL.md` |\n355\t| Web UI work (only when the user asked for UI work)            | `docs/skills/tunyt-web-design.md`                     |\n356\t| User asks to parallelize with commandcode, or 3+ scoped tasks | `.claude/skills/delegate-to-commandcode/SKILL.md`     |\n357\t\n358\t---\n359\t\n360\t## Production, in short\n361\t\n362\t- **One VPS, one Docker Swarm stack** (`docker-compose.prod.yaml`). One image,\n363\t  `adppandey/tunyt-api:<tag>`, runs as two services: `tunyt-api` (HTTP, `dist/bin.js`, cluster mode)\n364\t  and `tunyt-worker` (every BullMQ worker, AI included). Both load New Relic with `-r newrelic`.\n365\t- **nginx is the only public entry point.** Its rate-limit zones are in `nginx.conf`. The check-in\n366\t  routes deliberately have no `limit_req` and no `proxy_next_upstream`, because check-in isn't\n367\t  idempotent.\n368\t- **`apps/web` is deployed separately** (a Vercel-class host). CI only builds it.\n369\t- **CI** (`ci.yml`) runs typecheck, lint and build for server and web. **CD** (`deploy.yml`) runs on\n370\t  pushes to `main` that touch `apps/server/**`: build, push, `docker stack deploy`, a health gate on\n371\t  `/api/v1/health`, and native Swarm rollback if that fails.\n372\t- **Nothing runs migrations for you.** No CI step and no Dockerfile `CMD` runs `prisma migrate\n373\tdeploy`, and the prod image has no `prisma/` folder or CLI. Migrations reach prod only when the\n374\t  user runs them by hand. So every schema change ends with you telling the user to run\n375\t  `migrate status` and then `migrate deploy` against prod.\n376\t- Secrets live in the VPS `.env`. `docker stack deploy` doesn't auto-load it for interpolation.\n377\t\n378\t### Don't modify without an explicit request\n379\t\n380\t- `docker-compose.*.yaml`\n381\t- `nginx.conf`, `nginx-temp.conf`\n382\t- `apps/server/Dockerfile`\n383\t- `.github/workflows/**` and `.github/actions/telegram-notify`\n384\t- `scripts/acme-preflight.sh`\n385\t\n386\t---\n387\t\n388\t## Changelog\n389\t\n390\tAgents fill `CHANGELOG.md` themselves, no prompt needed:\n391\t\n392\t1. Add one line under `## [Unreleased]` in the right section (Added, Changed, Fixed, Removed,\n393\t   Security), written for a host or user reading release notes.\n394\t2. Format: `- **scope** What changed for the user (#PR)`. Scope is `server`, `web`, `crm`, `mobile`\n395\t   or `shared`. If the PR number isn't known yet, write `(#TBD)` and fill it once the PR is open.\n396\t3. Skip it only for refactors, tests, docs and CI with no visible effect, and say so in the hand-back.\n397\t4. Commit the changelog line in the same commit as the change it describes.\n398\t5. At release time (`stag` into `main`), rename `[Unreleased]` to the date and start a fresh one.\n399\t\n400\t---\n401\t\n402\t## Learned by melon\n403\t\n404\tShort, durable lessons that a tool appends here. Keep each one general (true for the next task, not\n405\tjust the last one) and move it into a proper section above once it's confirmed. One-off notes about\n406\ta finished feature don't belong here: the code already records them.\n407\t\n408\t- Don't claim a fix from an in-session simulation. Check that the change exists in the real code\n409\t  or app before reporting it done.\n410\t- A progress or loading indicator must actually complete. Don't ship a bar that never finishes.\n411\t- For page-changing navigation, give immediate feedback (prefetch or a transition state) rather\n412\t  than an intrusive button spinner, and lock the control until the navigation finishes so repeat\n413\t  taps don't fire twice.\n414\t\n415\t## Learned by zerd\n416\t\n417\t- On the create-event page, truncate the location address text so it cannot break the grid layout.\n418\t- Investigate why pasting a location link duplicates it in the create event page, and fix the paste handler so each link is inserted only once.\n419\t- Preserve the existing working location-link parsing behavior from the live version; when fixing paste handling, prevent the browser’s duplicate insertion without changing how links are parsed or broken down.\n420\t- When a review finds issues, apply the fixes rather than only reporting them, and verify the create-event and event-detail pages reflect the change.\n421\t- Don't report \"done\" until the work actually builds and survives rebase: verify the commits are on the branch (not dropped) and fix remaining issues before committing again.\n422\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dd825012-52aa-4f5b-b0f6-761df9f383e4","uuid":"421ac119-3912-4b12-b150-d665886bdc00","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:04:20.766Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/l9/28lkl3090p9dzbh6jvml0kkr0000gn/T/zerd-duel-zpf_oqz9/tunyt/AGENTS.md","content":"# AGENTS.md\n\nGuidance for AI coding agents working in this repository, whatever the harness (Claude Code,\ncommandcode, melon, Codex...). **These instructions override default behavior. Follow them exactly.**\n\nThis root file holds the rules that apply everywhere. Each app has a short `AGENTS.md` with its own\nrules; read it as soon as you start working in that folder (see _Repo map_).\n\n---\n\n## Absolute Rules (read these first, never break them)\n\nThese apply to every agent and every harness, in every folder, no matter what a skill or a\nnested `AGENTS.md` says. If anything else in this repo conflicts with them, these win.\n\n### 1. Never read a `.env` file\n\nDon't open, `cat`, grep, glob into, diff or summarize any `.env*` file: `.env`, `.env.local`,\n`.env.production`, `.env.example`, all of them. They hold real secrets, and even the example file\nis where people accidentally paste a real value.\n\nIf you need to know which variables exist, read the code that validates them instead\n(`apps/server/src/config/index.ts` for the server). If you need a _value_, ask the user to check\nit and tell you the answer. The same goes for any other secret file (`*.pem`, `*.key`, service\naccount JSON).\n\n### 2. Never touch the database. Hand the user the query.\n\nYou don't run SQL, you don't connect to a database, and you don't run any command whose job is to\nread or change one. That covers local, staging and production, with no exceptions for \"it's just a\nSELECT\".\n\nOff limits:\n\n- `psql`, `pg_dump`, `redis-cli FLUSH*`, GUI clients, `prisma studio`\n- `prisma migrate dev | deploy | status | resolve | reset`, `prisma db push | pull | execute | seed`\n- Ad-hoc `ts-node` / `tsx` scripts that import Prisma, and **everything in `apps/server/scripts/`**\n  (most of it is one-off repair scripts that write to the DB)\n- Starting the API, workers or e2e suites purely to poke at data. Ask first, since booting them\n  connects to the database.\n\nStill fine: reading and editing `schema.prisma` and migration files as text, `npx prisma generate`\n(it only writes the client, no DB connection), `tsc`, lint, builds and the pure-logic specs.\n\n**What to do instead:** write the query and give it to the user in a code block, and say three\nthings next to it:\n\n1. **Where to run it:** local, or prod (and say so loudly if it's prod).\n2. **Read or write:** a `SELECT` / `EXPLAIN` is read-only. Anything that changes data is called out\n   as a write, wrapped in `BEGIN; ... ROLLBACK;` by default so the user can inspect it before they\n   swap in `COMMIT;`.\n3. **What to paste back:** the columns or row counts you need to continue.\n\nExample of the shape to hand over:\n\n````md\nRun this on **prod** (read-only):\n\n```sql\nSELECT id, status, total FROM \"Booking\" WHERE id = '<bookingId>';\n```\n\nPaste me the row. I'm looking for `status` and whether `total` matches the payment amount.\n````\n\nFor schema changes, you write the `schema.prisma` edit and the migration file, then give the user\nthe exact `npx prisma migrate dev --name <name>` command to run themselves.\n\n### 3. Never print or echo secrets\n\nIf one shows up anyway (a stack trace, a pasted log, a config dump), don't repeat it in your\nreply, a commit message, a comment or a file. Refer to it by variable name.\n\n---\n\n## How to work here\n\n### Always on, from the first message\n\n- **graphify.** Orient with `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` before grepping raw files (see _Using\n  the graph_). If the graph is behind HEAD, run `graphify update .` first.\n- **ponytail (full).** Climb the ladder: does it need to exist, is it already in the repo, stdlib,\n  native platform, an installed dependency, then the minimum code. Fix the root cause where all\n  callers route through, not just the one the ticket names. It governs what you build, never the\n  checks: validation at trust boundaries, security, error handling that prevents data loss and\n  accessibility are never simplified away.\n- **`prompt.yaml`.** If the one at the repo root has a non-empty `objective`, it is the task. Read\n  it before anything else. Its `out_of_scope` and `approval` lists are hard stops (ask before\n  anything under `approval`). `type: review` and `type: question` mean read-only. Blank means\n  ignore it. CI resets it to `docs/prompt.template.yaml` after a merge. Format: `docs/prompt-yaml.md`.\n\n### Task flow\n\n1. **Orient.** Graph report first, then open only the files involved.\n2. **Read the matching skill** (table below) and the nested `AGENTS.md` for the folder.\n3. **Reuse check.** Grep for an existing helper, type, component or pattern before writing one.\n   Ask before adding a dependency.\n4. **Smallest change that fixes the root cause.** Keep scope exact. Leave CRM, mobile,\n   `infrastructure/` and unrelated files alone unless asked.\n5. **Verify** with real commands (per-app checks in the nested files and\n   `docs/skills/tunyt-verification.md`). Report the actual output, and say what you did not verify.\n   Run the existing specs, but don't write new ones during a fix round unless asked. Tests are\n   Playwright only, never vitest or jest.\n6. **Keep the repo in sync** without being asked: Bruno `.yml` for API changes (`BrunoCollection/`\n   at the repo root), `graphify update .` after code changes, and the changelog line.\n7. **Hand back** in a few lines, then ask: _\"This part is done, should I commit it?\"_\n\n### When to ask and when to just act\n\nAsk first:\n\n- Before writing a spec, a plan or a design doc. Never produce one by default. When you do write\n  one, show it as a Lavish artifact if the harness has the `lavish` skill.\n- Before any visual change (the UI Guard below).\n- Before booting the API, workers or e2e (they connect to the DB), adding a dependency, or anything\n  hard to undo.\n- When a feature request is broad or ambiguous. Look at the existing APIs and flows first, then ask\n  specific questions.\n\nJust act:\n\n- **A bug report means fix it.** Explain the cause in two or three lines, then apply the fix in the\n  same turn. Don't stop at a root-cause analysis or a verdict.\n- **Security findings are the exception:** explain each one in plain words first and wait.\n- Execution details (which branch, worktree or not, how to split commits): pick the sensible\n  default from this file and go.\n- Asked for a command or a query? Give the text. Don't run the workflow.\n\n### UI Guard (`apps/web`, and `apps/crm` if it is ever touched)\n\nAsk the user before you:\n\n- add a visible component, page, section or route\n- restyle anything (color, spacing, layout, typography)\n- change user-facing copy, labels, or the order of visible elements\n- swap icons or imagery\n\nYou can go ahead without asking for: an obvious visual bug (broken layout, overflow), non-visual\nlogic inside an existing component (handlers, state, API calls), import or type fixes after a\nrename, and removing confirmed-unused code. When unsure, ask. Ten seconds beats rework.\n\n### Git and commits\n\n- **Branches:** day-to-day work lands on `stag`. `main` is protected and only gets `stag` at release\n  time. A feature branch, when one is asked for, opens its PR into `stag`.\n- **Before any branch operation** (switch, rebase, reset, merge), look at the recent commits on both\n  sides and keep the newer work. Never reset onto a stale branch.\n- **Stash only what you mean to.** There are many old stashes. Use `git stash push -- <paths>`, never\n  a bare `git stash`, and say which stash entry you created.\n- **Never commit, stage or push without asking.** Once the user says yes, commit **in parts**: one\n  small commit per concern (for example: server fix, web hook, Bruno, changelog). Check both staged\n  and unstaged files so each commit holds only its own change.\n- **Commit messages** never mention a person's or an assistant's name or email. No `Co-Authored-By`.\n- Never use `--no-verify`, `--no-gpg-sign`, or amend published commits unless explicitly asked.\n- Always commit a filled-in `prompt.yaml` with the task's changes (its own small commit is fine).\n  CI logs it and resets it after merge, so never leave it out or ask whether to include it.\n- graphify output goes in its own commit: `GRAPH_REPORT.md`, `graph.json`, `manifest.json`. Never\n  commit `graphify-out/cache/`.\n\n### Code comments\n\nWrite comments the way a teammate would explain the code out loud. Keep them readable, and when a\ncomment is long, lead with a concrete example. Never use the `§` character in comments.\n\n```ts\n// Payouts wait a day after the event ends, so late refunds land first.\n// Example: an event ending Sat 23:00 gets its payout created Sun 23:00.\n```\n\n### Subagents\n\nUse parallel subagents when the harness has them and the work splits cleanly (one per app, or\nimplement and review in parallel). A prompt that says \"find gotchas\" gets generic advice back. A\nsharp prompt has a confirmed example as a template, a cap (\"5 to 10 findings\"), the format\n`file:line + wrong + right + why + severity`, and \"skip generic best practices\". If a subagent's\nclaim contradicts your own search, verify it with one targeted grep before you rely on it.\n\n---\n\n## Done checklist\n\n1. The per-app checks pass, run in this session: `npx tsc --noEmit` and `pnpm build` in\n   `apps/server`; `pnpm lint` and `pnpm typecheck` in `apps/web`; plus the existing Playwright\n   specs for the area.\n2. UI changes were checked in a real browser by repeating the user's action, not only with\n   typecheck or curl. If the browser extension isn't connected, drive it with the repo's\n   Playwright. If Playwright says browsers are missing, run `pnpm exec playwright install` first.\n3. Bruno `.yml` added or updated for any endpoint that was added, changed or removed.\n4. `security-testing-compliance` skill done if payment, auth or sensitive data was touched.\n5. UI Guard respected.\n6. `CHANGELOG.md` line added, or you said why none is needed (see _Changelog_).\n7. `graphify update .` run from the repo root.\n8. You never read a `.env*` file and never ran a DB command. Anything that needed the DB went to the\n   user as a query.\n9. You asked the user whether to commit.\n\nNever write \"should work\" or \"tests pass\" unless you ran them in this session. If you couldn't run\nsomething (DB, env, browser), say so instead of implying it passed.\n\n---\n\n## Using the graph\n\n`graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` has the community hubs and god nodes. `graphify-out/graph.json` is\nthe raw graph for deeper traversal. If `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` exists, navigate it first.\n\n- **Ask with specific names.** `set()`, `get()`, `GET()`, `POST()`, `parse()` and `dispatch()` merge\n  unrelated code into one node. Ask about `BookingService` or `wrapDatabaseOperation`, not `set`.\n- **Trust `EXTRACTED` edges, double-check `INFERRED` ones.** A `semantically_similar_to` edge is a\n  hint to go read the file, never proof. Example: `upcomingEventsPath()` linked to `set()` in a\n  payouts component is a name collision, not a dependency.\n- **Scope is server + web + shared.** `apps/crm`, `apps/mobile`, `infrastructure/`, tests, scripts,\n  email templates and generated code are excluded via `.graphifyignore`. \"Nothing calls this\" from\n  the graph proves nothing about those folders.\n- **Change the scope in `.graphifyignore`,** never by hand-editing `graph.json`. Run `/graphify` for\n  a full rebuild only when docs or the scope change. Otherwise `graphify update .` (AST only, free).\n\nA graph answer is a lead, not a fact. Before acting on one:\n\n1. **Is it fresh?** Compare the last build with `git log -1`, update if code moved on. After renames\n   or deletes, confirm the old symbol is really gone from `graph.json` (ghost nodes happen).\n2. **Does the target exist?** Open the file and read the lines the graph cited\n   (`source_file` + `source_location`). If it isn't there, update the graph, don't work around it.\n3. **Cross-check callers with one grep** across `apps/server`, `apps/web` and `packages/` before\n   renaming, deleting or changing a signature. Graph edges miss dynamic imports and string-keyed\n   lookups (queue names, cache keys, route paths). If grep and graph disagree, grep wins.\n4. **Bigger blast radius, stronger proof.** Reading needs steps 1 to 2. Editing needs 1 to 3 plus the\n   done checklist. Deleting, renaming, payment, auth or migration changes also need the security\n   skill where it applies and a user check before anything hard to reverse.\n\n---\n\n## Repo map\n\n**Tunyt** is an event ticketing platform: a pnpm 9 + Turborepo monorepo, Biome for lint and format,\nPlaywright for every test.\n\n| Folder                  | What it is                                                                                                  | Rules file                        |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `apps/server`           | Express 5 + Prisma 7 API and BullMQ workers. Payments, notifications, events, and the in-process AI flows.  | `apps/server/AGENTS.md`           |\n| `apps/web`              | Next.js 16 + React 19 site: discovery, booking, accounts, host dashboard, venues, checker, door staff, PWA. | `apps/web/AGENTS.md`              |\n| `packages/tunyt-shared` | `@tunyt/shared` types and helpers used by web and mobile (not the server).                                  | `packages/tunyt-shared/AGENTS.md` |\n| `apps/mobile`           | Expo app. Out of scope unless asked.                                                                        | `apps/mobile/AGENTS.md`           |\n\nEvery `CLAUDE.md` in the repo is a one-line `@AGENTS.md` import. Edit the `AGENTS.md`, never the\n`CLAUDE.md`. If a nested file disagrees with this one, this one wins, and you fix the drift.\n\nThere is no separate AI service. The event-draft and event-assistant flows live in\n`apps/server/src/lib/ai/` (pure code) and `services/ai/`, and run inside the worker process. Details\nin `apps/server/src/services/ai/README.md`.\n\n### Commands\n\n```bash\npnpm dev                                        # all apps in watch mode\npnpm lint && pnpm check-types                   # what the pre-push hook runs\ndocker compose -f docker-compose.local.yaml up -d   # local Redis, Postgres 17, Prometheus, Grafana\n```\n\nPer-app commands are in each nested file. Run commands from the repo root unless the nested file\nsays otherwise, and quote bracketed Next.js paths (`'apps/web/src/app/events/[eventId]/page.tsx'`).\n\n### Inactive paths (don't rely on these)\n\n- **`apps/crm`**: the old \"Tunyt Ops\" admin dashboard. Not built by CI, not deployed, not used. Host\n  tooling lives in `apps/web` now. Leave it alone unless the user asks.\n- **`infrastructure/`**: an old k3s + AWS plan that was never deployed. Don't use it to explain how\n  production works.\n- **`docker-compose.stag.yaml`**: mostly commented out, used by no workflow.\n- **`services/*`** in `pnpm-workspace.yaml`: the folder doesn't exist.\n\n---\n\n## Rules that apply across apps\n\nThese come from real bugs and real corrections. The full, confidence-scored list lives in\n`.commandcode/taste/` (`taste.md` plus `workflow/`, `ui/`, `design/`). Read it before improving a\nskill, a doc or a UI, and commit taste files along with the change they relate to. Where a taste\nfile disagrees with this file, this file wins.\n\n**How the business works**\n\n- **Every payment goes through Tunyt's own Razorpay account.** The per-host key code\n  (`lib/razorpay-factory.ts`, `razorpay-config.repository.ts`) is legacy: don't build on it or\n  extend it. There is no RazorpayX.\n- **Tunyt doesn't hold host money.** Payouts are created 24 hours after the event ends\n  (`PAYOUT_DELAY_HOURS` in `apps/server/src/utils/payout.util.ts`).\n- **Use Razorpay's native UPI links and QR codes**, not custom payment infrastructure.\n- **Users buy tickets, not seats.** Say \"ticket\" in every piece of user-facing copy.\n\n**Data and numbers**\n\n- Money is integer paise internally. Round only at the charge or payment boundary.\n- \"N sold\" counts tickets with `status = SUCCESS`, never a stored counter.\n- Fix counters and aggregates across every state transition (create, update, status change), not\n  just the one reported.\n- Event timing comes from start and end date-times: _upcoming_ means it starts in the future,\n  _live_ means it has started and not ended, _past_ means it has ended. Never classify with a bare\n  `date <= now`. A hosted event stays visible until its end time passes.\n- Carry `timezoneOffsetMinutes` with every date/time so the client renders the host's wall-clock\n  time. Never rely on the browser's or Node's implicit timezone.\n- Filters change the data, not just the view: wire them through repository, service, controller,\n  query params and the frontend hook.\n- Analytics defaults to a 7-day window (from = 6 days ago, to = 1 day after today). Date-filtered\n  queries skip the cache; only all-time results are cached.\n- Venue resources default `feeBornBy` to `\"USER\"`.\n- Extract shared utils and constants instead of duplicating them. Fix a value once, at its source.\n\n**Performance and debugging**\n\n- Fix for production scale: the bulk or batched path, not just the single-item case.\n- Optimize a slow query before raising a timeout or a TTL.\n- Silent API failures: check nginx `limit_req` and `proxy_next_upstream` retries before app code\n  (retries plus cluster mode cause duplicate writes and swallowed 503s).\n- Production debugging scripts use shell or `redis-cli`, never Node (prod has no Node shell).\n- Give each parallel test its own entity ID so shared cache keys don't collide.\n\n**Reviews**\n\n- Read the actual diff. Report only high-confidence findings, each with file, line, impact and a\n  concrete fix. Correctness, edge cases and race conditions come before infra concerns.\n- Marketing or landing pages also get an SEO pass (meta, headings, SSR vs CSR, alt text, LCP).\n- When fixing review findings, change application code only. Leave the Bruno files alone.\n\n**Web and UI** (the UI Guard still applies)\n\n- Server Components by default; `\"use client\"` only for state, effects, events or browser-only libs.\n- No emojis in UI, use the icon library. Dashboards stay monochrome white and gray, and any\n  gradient uses the app's own theme palette.\n- Modals cover every state: form, submitting, success, error. Prefer bottom sheets on mobile.\n- Mobile-first: one responsive card grid, not cards on mobile and a table on desktop.\n- Empty list pages carry a CTA to create the first item.\n- Show the specific error reason, never \"some error occurred\".\n- Filter and category options come from the data, not a hardcoded list.\n- In-app navigation (logo, errors, not-found, logout) goes to `/discover`, not `/`. The canonical\n  domain is `www.tunyt.com`. Page changes update their analytics events in the same change.\n- New users always see the username confirmation step. Never auto-accept a generated username.\n- Demos go out as one self-contained HTML file, with all JS and CSS inlined.\n\n---\n\n## Skills: read the matching one before you act\n\nThe canonical, tool-neutral skills live in `docs/skills/*.md`. `.claude/skills/` has thin wrappers\nfor Claude that point at the same files. Skills stack: a debugging session on a payment path reads\nthe debugging skill and the security skill, and every task ends with verification.\n\n| Trigger                                                       | Skill                                                 |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Any bug, 500, failing test, stuck queue job, slowness         | `docs/skills/tunyt-debugging.md`                      |\n| New list endpoint, Prisma query, cache, worker or data fetch  | `docs/skills/tunyt-performance.md`                    |\n| Before claiming any task done, before merge or deploy         | `docs/skills/tunyt-verification.md`                   |\n| Backend API change (route, controller, service, repo, types)  | `.claude/skills/api-conventions/SKILL.md`             |\n| Payment, auth or sensitive-data change                        | `.claude/skills/security-testing-compliance/SKILL.md` |\n| Web UI work (only when the user asked for UI work)            | `docs/skills/tunyt-web-design.md`                     |\n| User asks to parallelize with commandcode, or 3+ scoped tasks | `.claude/skills/delegate-to-commandcode/SKILL.md`     |\n\n---\n\n## Production, in short\n\n- **One VPS, one Docker Swarm stack** (`docker-compose.prod.yaml`). One image,\n  `adppandey/tunyt-api:<tag>`, runs as two services: `tunyt-api` (HTTP, `dist/bin.js`, cluster mode)\n  and `tunyt-worker` (every BullMQ worker, AI included). Both load New Relic with `-r newrelic`.\n- **nginx is the only public entry point.** Its rate-limit zones are in `nginx.conf`. The check-in\n  routes deliberately have no `limit_req` and no `proxy_next_upstream`, because check-in isn't\n  idempotent.\n- **`apps/web` is deployed separately** (a Vercel-class host). CI only builds it.\n- **CI** (`ci.yml`) runs typecheck, lint and build for server and web. **CD** (`deploy.yml`) runs on\n  pushes to `main` that touch `apps/server/**`: build, push, `docker stack deploy`, a health gate on\n  `/api/v1/health`, and native Swarm rollback if that fails.\n- **Nothing runs migrations for you.** No CI step and no Dockerfile `CMD` runs `prisma migrate\ndeploy`, and the prod image has no `prisma/` folder or CLI. Migrations reach prod only when the\n  user runs them by hand. So every schema change ends with you telling the user to run\n  `migrate status` and then `migrate deploy` against prod.\n- Secrets live in the VPS `.env`. `docker stack deploy` doesn't auto-load it for interpolation.\n\n### Don't modify without an explicit request\n\n- `docker-compose.*.yaml`\n- `nginx.conf`, `nginx-temp.conf`\n- `apps/server/Dockerfile`\n- `.github/workflows/**` and `.github/actions/telegram-notify`\n- `scripts/acme-preflight.sh`\n\n---\n\n## Changelog\n\nAgents fill `CHANGELOG.md` themselves, no prompt needed:\n\n1. Add one line under `## [Unreleased]` in the right section (Added, Changed, Fixed, Removed,\n   Security), written for a host or user reading release notes.\n2. Format: `- **scope** What changed for the user (#PR)`. Scope is `server`, `web`, `crm`, `mobile`\n   or `shared`. If the PR number isn't known yet, write `(#TBD)` and fill it once the PR is open.\n3. Skip it only for refactors, tests, docs and CI with no visible effect, and say so in the hand-back.\n4. Commit the changelog line in the same commit as the change it describes.\n5. At release time (`stag` into `main`), rename `[Unreleased]` to the date and start a fresh one.\n\n---\n\n## Learned by melon\n\nShort, durable lessons that a tool appends here. Keep each one general (true for the next task, not\njust the last one) and move it into a proper section above once it's confirmed. One-off notes about\na finished feature don't belong here: the code already records them.\n\n- Don't claim a fix from an in-session simulation. Check that the change exists in the real code\n  or app before reporting it done.\n- A progress or loading indicator must actually complete. Don't ship a bar that never finishes.\n- For page-changing navigation, give immediate feedback (prefetch or a transition state) rather\n  than an intrusive button spinner, and lock the control until the navigation finishes so repeat\n  taps don't fire twice.\n\n## Learned by zerd\n\n- On the create-event page, truncate the location address text so it cannot break the grid layout.\n- Investigate why pasting a location link duplicates it in the create event page, and fix the paste handler so each link is inserted only once.\n- Preserve the existing working location-link parsing behavior from the live version; when fixing paste handling, prevent the browser’s duplicate insertion without changing how links are parsed or broken down.\n- When a review finds issues, apply the fixes rather than only reporting them, and verify the create-event and event-detail pages reflect the change.\n- Don't report \"done\" until the work actually builds and survives rebase: verify the commits are on the branch (not dropped) and fix remaining issues before committing again.\n","numLines":422,"startLine":1,"totalLines":422}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call-c71fd807-a379-4e02-91c7-74b106cf66de","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call-bdbe1a05-dd24-49d7-ac9d-bbb2b6ceb49c","type":"tool_result","content":"/private/var/folders/l9/28lkl3090p9dzbh6jvml0kkr0000gn/T/zerd-duel-zpf_oqz9/tunyt\ntotal 2296\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 51 aditya  staff    1632 Nov 21 00:33 .\ndrwx------@  3 aditya  staff      96 Nov 21 00:33 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 aditya  staff      96 Nov 21 00:33 .agents\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff      78 Nov 21 00:33 .biomeignore\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 aditya  staff     128 Nov 21 00:33 .claude\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 aditya  staff     160 Nov 21 00:33 .codex\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 aditya  staff     160 Nov 21 00:33 .commandcode\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff      61 Nov 21 00:33 .git\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 aditya  staff     160 Nov 21 00:33 .github\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff     729 Nov 21 00:33 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff    1191 Nov 21 00:33 .graphifyignore\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 aditya  staff     160 Nov 21 00:34 .husky\ndrwxr-xr-x@  8 aditya  staff     256 Nov 21 00:33 .lavish\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 aditya  staff     128 Nov 21 00:33 .melon\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff       0 Nov 21 00:33 .npmrc\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 aditya  staff      96 Nov 21 00:33 .pi\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 aditya  staff      96 Nov 21 00:33 .superpowers\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 aditya  staff     128 Nov 21 00:33 .vscode\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 aditya  staff     128 Nov 21 00:33 .zerd\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff   24139 Nov 21 00:33 AGENTS.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff   63954 Nov 21 00:33 API_DOCUMENTATION.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@  6 aditya  staff     192 Nov 21 00:33 apps\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff   22688 Nov 21 00:33 AUDIT_FINDINGS.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff     589 Nov 21 00:33 biome.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff      40 Nov 21 00:33 blacklist.conf\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 62 aditya  staff    1984 Nov 21 00:33 BrunoCollection\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff   10549 Nov 21 00:33 CHANGELOG.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff      11 Nov 21 00:33 CLAUDE.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff    3256 Nov 21 00:33 docker-compose.local.yaml\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff   11523 Nov 21 00:33 docker-compose.prod.yaml\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff    1484 Nov 21 00:33 docker-compose.stag.yaml\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 13 aditya  staff     416 Nov 21 00:33 docs\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 42 aditya  staff    1344 Nov 21 00:33 graphify-out\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 19 aditya  staff     608 Nov 21 00:33 infrastructure\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 aditya  staff     288 Nov 21 00:33 monitoring\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff    1857 Nov 21 00:33 nginx-temp.conf\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff   25317 Nov 21 00:33 nginx.conf\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 25 aditya  staff     800 Nov 21 00:34 node_modules\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff    1180 Nov 21 00:33 package.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 aditya  staff      96 Nov 21 00:33 packages\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff   14637 Nov 21 00:33 PerformanceAudit.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff  892586 Nov 21 00:33 pnpm-lock.yaml\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff      57 Nov 21 00:33 pnpm-workspace.yaml\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff   14403 Nov 21 00:33 ProductionDeployment.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff    5556 Nov 21 00:33 prompt.yaml\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff    7817 Nov 21 00:33 README.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 aditya  staff     160 Nov 21 00:33 scripts\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff     247 Nov 21 00:33 skills-lock.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff    1904 Nov 21 00:33 test-for-razorpay.html\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff     708 Nov 21 00:33 TROUBLESHOOTING.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 aditya  staff     773 Nov 21 00:33 turbo.json\nNot currently on any branch.\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\n7016e9d0f cleanup\n05f4976e6 style(changelog): keep the app update notes together\n6dbab213a feat(web): give the installed app a native feel\ne6090b0c5 feat(web): ask before reloading for a new app version\n7f8c10762 fix(web): point PWA shortcuts at routes that exist","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dd825012-52aa-4f5b-b0f6-761df9f383e4","uuid":"46f7f06a-3fd1-4a12-b767-bf1c33abc5bd","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:04:22.604Z","tool_u